PHYSICS & DAMAGE RULES
Aircraft are overweight and underpowered
Wings flex beyond tolerance
Rivet lines vibrate, partially unzip, then re-seat
Control surfaces lag before responding
One engine intermittently misfires — torque imbalance visible

FIRE & SMOKE (CONTROLLED)
Small fires only
internal engine glow
burning fuel mist along panel seams
Smoke is:
thin
dark
directional (dragged by airflow)
NEVER billowing clouds
Fire flickers under wind pressure, not cinematic flames
DEBRIS BEHAVIOR
Screws, wiring, panels tear off mid-flight
Pieces fall quietly, not explosively
Camera occasionally follows debris for 0.4–0.6s before cutting away

Nothing floats unless forced.
Everything obeys inertia.

